      "message": "Throughout `bootrom.cc` and `ec_comm.cc`, there are many instances of casting structs to `uint8_t` spans.\n\n**Current Pattern:**\n\n```c\nEgisBootrom::SystemResetCommand req;\nstd::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e req_span(reinterpret_cast\u003cconst uint8_t *\u003e(\u0026req), sizeof(req));\nauto resp \u003d SendBootromCommand(req_span);\n\n```\n\nUsing `reinterpret_cast` directly in business logic violates the principle of keeping type-punning isolated. You can completely DRY this up by adding a helper to `egis_util.h` and a generic send method to `BootromComm`.\n\n**The Fix:** Add a byte-casting helper in `egis_util.h`:\n\n```c\ntemplate \u003cTriviallyCopyable T\u003e\nstd::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e AsBytes(const T\u0026 obj) {\n  return {reinterpret_cast\u003cconst uint8_t*\u003e(\u0026obj), sizeof(T)};\n}\n\n```\n\nAdd a template wrapper in `bootrom.h`:\n\n```c\ntemplate \u003ctypename T\u003e\nstd::expected\u003cstd::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e, BootromError\u003e SendStruct(\n    const T\u0026 command, \n    std::chrono::milliseconds timeout \u003d kDefaultCommandTimeout) {\n  return SendBootromCommand(AsBytes(command), timeout);\n}\n\n```\n\n**Resulting Clean Code (in `bootrom.cc`):**\n\n```c\nEgisBootrom::SystemResetCommand req;\nauto resp \u003d SendStruct(req); // Replaces 3 lines with 2, no casts!\n\n```",
